/-!
# VIII10 — M1: two-sided bounds on the compact probes from the genuine integrals

On the closed compact window `KG = [0, 1/3]` and `t ∈ [0,1]` the denominator satisfies
`2/3 ≤ 1 - t x ≤ 1`, hence `(1 - t x)⁻¹ ≥ 1` and `(1 - t x)⁻² ≥ 1`.  Comparing the
actual integrands `1`, `t`, `t²` pointwise and integrating gives

  `1 ≤ Hc x`, `1/2 ≤ Gc x`, `1/3 ≤ GcD x`,

and `Hc = 1 + x Gc` with `x ≤ 1/3`, `Gc ≤ 3/4` gives `Hc x ≤ 5/4`.

Both endpoints are handled: `x = 0` is spatial infinity, `x = 1/3` the background horizon
(`KG ⊂ UG`).  Nothing here is sampled or continued; the bounds are integral comparisons against
the real `J`-integrands.
-/

